{
  "_note": [
    "Case definitions for scripts/test-hook-contract (CB-127).",
    "",
    "Each case names a hook script, the stdin payload it receives, and the",
    "project state it runs against. The recorded exit code and stderr live",
    "in tests/golden/hook-contract.json and are the contract CB-128 must",
    "preserve while it moves the refusal into a host adapter.",
    "",
    "state is a list of tokens applied to the throwaway project:",
    "  run-active    the run-active flag is armed",
    "  run-complete  the run-complete marker is present",
    "  careful       destructive-command's opt-in flag",
    "  boundary      edit-boundary's opt-in flag",
    "  run-context   a run directory under context/ holding a plan",
    "  exec-log      that run directory holding an edit ledger",
    "  contracts     memory/contracts/ exists",
    "",
    "  check-command  a check command registered for the backend surface",
    "A case that records exit 0 for every version of the code proves",
    "nothing. Each guard therefore carries both an allowed path and the",
    "path where it refuses.",
    "",
    "Known gap. skill-floor, reach-floor, contract-floor and digest-cap are",
    "recorded on their allowed path only: arming them needs a skill ledger,",
    "a reachability report, a contract and a transcript respectively, which",
    "a synthetic project cannot produce cheaply. Their refusal paths stay",
    "covered by their own suites (test-exec-floor, test-reachability,",
    "test-contract-check, test-skill-selection). This file says so rather",
    "than letting four exit-0 rows look like coverage.",
    "",
    "CB-146 added SessionStart and four cases for it. The golden was",
    "re-taken deliberately, which is the only way it is ever re-taken: the",
    "binding gained an event, so the frozen file described a tree that no",
    "longer exists. A re-capture without a task saying why is the failure",
    "this file guards against."
  ],
